steps.detail:
Keep going until:
- the child shows an obvious sign of life, such as breathing normally or moving;
- an AED is ready to use;
- another trained person takes over;
- medical help arrives and takes over;
- you are alone and too exhausted to continue;
- the scene becomes unsafe;
- you are alone, have done about 2 minutes of CPR, and decide to go for help (AHA 2025 pediatric single-rescuer algorithm).
